<title>JAPAN: Japan two-yr note auction lowest price of 100.09.</title>
<headline>Japan two-yr note auction lowest price of 100.09.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The auction of 120 billion yen in 0.9 percent two-year government notes produced the following results, the Ministry of Finance said on Friday:</p>
<p>Lowest price	 100.09    Stop rate	   0.854 pct</p>
<p>Average price	100.11    Average yield     0.839 pct</p>
<p>Total bids	   292.9 billion yen</p>
<p>Accepted Bids	119.3 billion yen</p>
<p>Bids accepted at lowest price 5.4726 pct</p>
<p>Issue date    August 20, 1997   Maturity    August 20, 1999</p>
